14
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.560
MSD, Ministry of Social Development, Public Trust,

15
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.460
the health system, and New Zealand Police.

16
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.220
Caitlin was brave, ethical, articulate, and persevering.

17
00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.180
She stood up for herself.

18
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.400
People found that difficult.

19
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.440
Caitlin lived in miserable, unhealthy, and unsafe conditions, sleeping in

20
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.240
parks until moved on or abused by neighbors, in derelict

21
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.170
houses, or taken in by people who professed to help her but preyed on

22
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:13.420
her.

23
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.110
She was abused, attacked, assaulted, and stolen from

24
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.660
repeatedly. My daughter survived less than two years

25
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.800
homeless, dying at half the age of both her grandmothers.

26
00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.300
Homeless people die 30 years early.

27
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.140
Caitlin wrote that the previous year hospital told her that if she

28
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.160
continued to live outdoors in winter, she would not survive to spring.

29
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.030
Family and others slept in that winter.

30
00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:44.560
As recent New Zealand research finds, homeless people die 30 years

31
00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.220
earlier than the rest of us with a roof over our heads.

32
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.100
And to quote from that report, "Premature mortality results

33
00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:56.000
from a complex combination of medical conditions, often related

34
00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.910
to severe and chronic comorbidities, and the consequences of

35
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.680
