392
00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:14.340
Are you identifying with the business owners who want to get rid of these

393
00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:17.910
people, who don't actually care what happens to them as long as they're out of

394
00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:18.520
their sight?

395
00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:20.880
Under this bill,

396
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.400
I guess you would call the cops. Shame on you.

397
00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:29.200
If you can excuse and work alongside perpetrators of violence

398
00:22:29.240 --> 00:22:33.069
yourselves, perpetrators who haven't had a day of adversity in their lives,

399
00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:37.510
perhaps you could excuse people for talking aloud to themselves, for

400
00:22:37.619 --> 00:22:41.290
sleeping on the street, for begging, for lashing out, for

401
00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:45.300
scaring people when they're experiencing the most difficult conditions to

402
00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:48.480
be found in this country under reprehensible economic

403
00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:52.380
management. Our economy doesn't function for

404
00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.260
the sake of your rich friends. It's for all of us.

405
00:22:56.780 --> 00:23:00.730
If there are people who can't sleep in their own safe and warm homes, it is

406
00:23:00.780 --> 00:23:01.580
truly broken.

407
00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:05.940
Why should I, simply as a human with a heart, feel more

408
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:08.680
responsibility towards the homeless and vulnerable than you?

409
00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:13.840
I guess because I imagine my role in my community as caring

410
00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:17.740
for, loving, and protecting others, and you think of your role as something

411
00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:21.280
else entirely. Protecting legal economic exchange, I guess.

412
00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:26.460
I don't want the community, the economy, or the world that this bill

413
00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:29.240
imagines. I hate it, and I reject it.

414
00:23:29.980 --> 00:23:33.960
If you support this bill through this process, I tell you, if you still have

415
00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:37.320
one, there is so, so, so much work to be done on your heart.

416
00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:39.680
Thank you. I'll take questions.

417
00:23:39.880 --> 00:23:42.360
Thank you, Kyle. We have a question from Dan Rosewarne.

418
00:23:42.780 --> 00:23:44.720
Thanks, Kyle. I appreciate that submission.

419
00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:47.740
I found this passage in your submission particularly interesting.

420
00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:52.080
"Conversation, donation, and other interaction with homeless and

421
00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:56.020
otherwise vulnerable people reminds me that I'm part of a community."

422
00:23:57.280 --> 00:24:00.280
Your submission talks about homelessness as something that affects the whole

423
00:24:00.300 --> 00:24:03.480
community rather than something that sits outside of it.

424
00:24:04.840 --> 00:24:08.790
And my question is, how do you think legislation like this changes

425
00:24:08.820 --> 00:24:12.620
the way the public sees people experiencing homelessness?

426
00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:17.080
It's just horrific because you think that if you feel a negative response when you

427
00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:20.660
see a homeless person, what that negative response really is, is

428
00:24:20.720 --> 00:24:24.420
guilt and shame and sadness. It should be sadness and empathy.

429
00:24:24.450 --> 00:24:27.860
And if this bill passes, what it's going to be is fear.

430
00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:31.220
It's going to be blaming that person for what's happening to them, and it's wanting

431
00:24:31.260 --> 00:24:35.192
to get rid of them So I think that you are twisting the basic empathetic

432
00:24:35.272 --> 00:24:38.642
responses of human beings in their communities, and you're telling them to call the

433
00:24:38.692 --> 00:24:41.672
cops on people that they should be reaching out to help and protect.

434
00:24:42.412 --> 00:24:42.652
Thank you.

435
00:24:43.012 --> 00:24:45.792
Thank you, Carl. Thank you very much for your written submission and for joining us

436
00:24:45.812 --> 00:24:46.812
this afternoon as well.

437
00:24:47.192 --> 00:24:50.402
Thank you. And I really support the submissions we had before as well, and that

438
00:24:50.432 --> 00:24:50.912
we're here following.

439
00:24:51.292 --> 00:24:51.712
Fantastic.

440
00:24:51.932 --> 00:24:51.982
Thank you.

