460
00:25:52.712 --> 00:25:55.352
The Law Society has significant concerns about this bill.

461
00:25:56.132 --> 00:25:59.692
We feel that it adopts a broad discretionary and coercive framework,

462
00:25:59.892 --> 00:26:02.832
and we feel that it infringes on several fundamental rights.

463
00:26:03.692 --> 00:26:07.672
It's therefore our recommendation that the bill not proceed, and we feel that even

464
00:26:07.712 --> 00:26:11.542
if significant changes are made, the bill is going to still remain fundamentally

465
00:26:11.552 --> 00:26:11.902
flawed.

466
00:26:13.212 --> 00:26:14.792
Just to highlight some of our concerns.

467
00:26:15.852 --> 00:26:19.342
The first is that we feel that the work undertaken by the Retail Ministry

468
00:26:19.392 --> 00:26:23.252
Advisory Group is not a substitute for a full policy development process,

469
00:26:23.832 --> 00:26:26.772
and it's clear from the risk impact statement that this has not happened.

470
00:26:27.772 --> 00:26:30.812
More work is needed, and more voices need to be heard before this bill can be

471
00:26:30.852 --> 00:26:31.432
justified.

472
00:26:32.952 --> 00:26:36.252
We note that in relation to the recent Trespass Bill, the views of the Ministry

473
00:26:36.932 --> 00:26:40.892
Advisory Group was not shared by other retail representatives, and

474
00:26:40.932 --> 00:26:41.792
that's a real problem.

475
00:26:43.072 --> 00:26:47.012
Second, we're concerned that while this bill is clearly intended to work alongside

476
00:26:47.052 --> 00:26:50.992
the Trespass Specific Retail Premises and Other Matters Amendment bill,

477
00:26:51.442 --> 00:26:53.321
the two are being considered separately in committee.

478
00:26:54.232 --> 00:26:57.552
We feel that the only way for the committee, for Parliament, and for the public to

479
00:26:57.632 --> 00:27:00.892
truly understand the combined effect of these two bills is for them to be

480
00:27:00.912 --> 00:27:01.772
considered together.

481
00:27:02.752 --> 00:27:05.252
Both of them suffer from the same lack of policy development,

482
00:27:06.132 --> 00:27:09.992
and they allow people who engage in conduct that is undesirable but not

483
00:27:10.052 --> 00:27:10.532
