2224
03:05:02.664 --> 03:05:05.904
Just to introduce ourselves, this is Bishop Anna.

2225
03:05:05.944 --> 03:05:08.564
She's Assistant Bishop of Wellington. I'm Justin.

2226
03:05:08.644 --> 03:05:11.884
I'm the Senior Bishop of Wellington. We represent the Wellington Diocese.

2227
03:05:13.384 --> 03:05:15.504
Also we're here not just representing the Wellington Diocese,

2228
03:05:16.384 --> 03:05:19.404
we've both spent decades journeying alongside people,

2229
03:05:20.504 --> 03:05:23.564
young people and homeless people, particularly in Auckland, Whanganui, and

2230
03:05:23.604 --> 03:05:27.314
Wellington. And so we've spent time with these people as our friends, family, and

2231
03:05:27.364 --> 03:05:30.624
often as flatmates, et cetera. So we bring in that perspective as well.

2232
03:05:31.964 --> 03:05:35.624
Kia ora koutou. We know that you've already heard from many others from

2233
03:05:35.664 --> 03:05:39.284
across the Christian tradition, and they have shared with you our belief

2234
03:05:39.724 --> 03:05:42.804
that every person has inherent dignity and value.

2235
03:05:43.364 --> 03:05:47.324
They've also shared with you that the Jesus we follow treated those

2236
03:05:47.344 --> 03:05:50.524
that his own society discarded and disregarded

2237
03:05:51.724 --> 03:05:55.284
in complete contrast to the way that his society treated them, with compassion,

2238
03:05:55.414 --> 03:05:59.324
with dignity, and with care. We follow the Jesus who declared

2239
03:05:59.333 --> 03:06:01.664
that he had come to bring good news to the poor.

2240
03:06:02.184 --> 03:06:06.164
We follow the Jesus who, when called upon by a beggar in the street, did

2241
03:06:06.284 --> 03:06:10.244
not silence that beggar like others in the crowd tried to, but instead

2242
03:06:10.284 --> 03:06:13.724
invited that beggar to come forward and said, "What do you want me to do for you?"

2243
03:06:14.684 --> 03:06:18.624
And in response to the beggar's reply, Jesus healed him from his blindness.

2244
03:06:19.324 --> 03:06:23.004
Our faith calls us, as followers of Jesus, to respond to

2245
03:06:23.044 --> 03:06:26.944
those in need, those in poverty, those in distress with

2246
03:06:26.964 --> 03:06:30.344
the same way that Jesus did, with compassion, with care,

2247
03:06:30.904 --> 03:06:31.764
and with dignity.

2248
03:06:32.964 --> 03:06:36.734
And while our faith provides us with a very strong basis for opposing this bill,

2249
03:06:37.224 --> 03:06:38.284
the main reasons that we

2250
03:06:39.244 --> 03:06:43.024
oppose it are on the grounds of common sense and on the ground of the

2251
03:06:43.104 --> 03:06:43.644
common good.

2252
03:06:44.504 --> 03:06:48.484
We want public spaces that are safe places for people.

2253
03:06:48.504 --> 03:06:52.404
The Summary Offences Act already contains offenses

2254
03:06:52.464 --> 03:06:54.444
for disorderly and aggressive behavior.

2255
03:06:55.014 --> 03:06:58.964
They are offenses because there is a real risk of harm to people

2256
03:06:59.004 --> 03:07:02.444
or property, and the police already have the powers that they

2257
03:07:02.484 --> 03:07:06.264
need to deal with such behaviors. The only new

2258
03:07:06.304 --> 03:07:10.064
behaviors, I'm using inverted commas here, being targeted

2259
03:07:10.224 --> 03:07:14.144
by the proposed bill are begging, rough sleeping, and an intention to

2260
03:07:14.324 --> 03:07:18.024
inhabit the public space. These are not a threat to

2261
03:07:18.044 --> 03:07:21.694
public safety. This bill treats the visible

2262
03:07:21.804 --> 03:07:25.304
presence of poverty as the problem rather than harmful behavior.

2263
03:07:25.624 --> 03:07:28.764
It shifts the focus from public safety to public

2264
03:07:28.984 --> 03:07:32.624
discomfort. And it appears that that is what this bill is really

2265
03:07:32.683 --> 03:07:35.344
about, appeasing our discomfort.

2266
03:07:35.804 --> 03:07:39.604
Because it's uncomfortable to see a fellow human being sleeping on a

2267
03:07:39.624 --> 03:07:43.384
park bench when many of us have a private, safe, and secure place to

2268
03:07:43.404 --> 03:07:47.104
return to each night. It is uncomfortable to see another human

2269
03:07:47.184 --> 03:07:51.084
being begging for spare change or a scrap of food as we

2270
03:07:51.144 --> 03:07:52.304
go about our business.

2271
03:07:53.784 --> 03:07:57.684
We should be discomforted by this reality, and we ought to

2272
03:07:57.764 --> 03:07:58.264
respond.

2273
03:07:59.304 --> 03:08:03.044
But how we choose to collectively respond in our discomfort says a lot

2274
03:08:03.104 --> 03:08:04.864
about who we are as a society.

2275
03:08:05.824 --> 03:08:09.704
This bill suggests that an appropriate response to a 14-year-old who is rough

2276
03:08:09.764 --> 03:08:13.644
sleeping or begging is to hand them a piece of paper that tells them to

2277
03:08:13.724 --> 03:08:17.704
move on, and to charge that 14-year-old if they fail to comply with that

2278
03:08:17.744 --> 03:08:21.584
order. That's not common sense. If a young person

2279
03:08:21.624 --> 03:08:25.434
is rough sleeping or experiencing deprivation to the extent that

2280
03:08:25.464 --> 03:08:29.424
they are begging, asking them to move on or charging them

2281
03:08:29.444 --> 03:08:33.084
for non-compliance ignores and further compounds that young person's

2282
03:08:33.124 --> 03:08:33.704
vulnerability.

2283
03:08:34.864 --> 03:08:38.804
Common sense says that if a 14-year-old is rough sleeping or begging, we ought

2284
03:08:38.844 --> 03:08:40.984
to be concerned about their care and protection.

2285
03:08:41.764 --> 03:08:45.264
Common sense suggests that the young person should be offered appropriate social,

2286
03:08:45.644 --> 03:08:49.204
wellbeing, and housing support. It's in the young person's best

2287
03:08:49.244 --> 03:08:53.204
interest, but it's also in the best interest of the common good to take

2288
03:08:53.304 --> 03:08:56.804
early preventative action that reduce the likelihood that young

2289
03:08:56.844 --> 03:09:00.644
person will experience long-term homelessness and all the

2290
03:09:00.684 --> 03:09:04.434
likely consequences of that, unemployment, poverty, addiction, poor

2291
03:09:04.564 --> 03:09:08.384
mental and physical health. Unfortunately, that's what the evidence

2292
03:09:08.504 --> 03:09:12.464
says are the predicted outcomes for young people experiencing

2293
03:09:12.504 --> 03:09:15.824
housing insecurity, especially for those who've been in state care

2294
03:09:17.216 --> 03:09:20.996
That same common sense principle applies to adults who are rough sleeping or

2295
03:09:21.016 --> 03:09:24.956
begging. Handing them a piece of paper that tells them to move on

2296
03:09:24.976 --> 03:09:28.796
does nothing to address the circumstances that led them there in the

2297
03:09:28.836 --> 03:09:32.536
first place, nor does it provide a bed, a meal, a friend,

2298
03:09:32.716 --> 03:09:36.566
mental health support, addiction treatment, or a pathway to housing.

2299
03:09:36.596 --> 03:09:40.396
What it does do is undermine the very initiatives that are already in place to

2300
03:09:40.436 --> 03:09:41.896
provide essential support

2301
03:09:42.776 --> 03:09:45.886
by shuffling the poor from one street to another.

2302
03:09:45.936 --> 03:09:47.016
That's not common sense.

2303
03:09:48.186 --> 03:09:52.176
Common sense tells us that if we want fewer people sleeping rough

2304
03:09:52.216 --> 03:09:56.036
or begging, we should continue to invest in the things that have proven to

2305
03:09:56.056 --> 03:09:59.746
reduce homelessness and poverty, stable housing, effective social

2306
03:09:59.796 --> 03:10:03.456
support, accessible health and addiction services, and support for at-risk children

2307
03:10:03.476 --> 03:10:07.116
and young people. The government claims it wants to invest in

2308
03:10:07.176 --> 03:10:10.056
solutions that actually work and are effective.

2309
03:10:10.116 --> 03:10:14.056
You have heard over and over again in these submissions from experts

2310
03:10:14.066 --> 03:10:17.536
telling you what the evidence is. Housing first works.

2311
03:10:18.056 --> 03:10:21.416
Providing accessibility to health and addiction services works.

2312
03:10:21.976 --> 03:10:25.836
Offering social supports work. The common good is

2313
03:10:25.876 --> 03:10:28.896
not served by making vulnerable people less visible.

2314
03:10:29.636 --> 03:10:32.096
It is served by reducing the vulnerability itself.

2315
03:10:32.976 --> 03:10:36.936
Public spaces become safer, not because we have moved people on, but

2316
03:10:36.956 --> 03:10:39.436
because more people have safe places to go.

2317
03:10:40.496 --> 03:10:44.206
Every day, on our streets, we come face to face with vulnerable

2318
03:10:44.316 --> 03:10:48.256
people facing poverty and homelessness, and we get to choose how we

2319
03:10:48.296 --> 03:10:48.736
respond.

2320
03:10:49.796 --> 03:10:53.406
This bill asks us to respond to begging and rough sleeping by

2321
03:10:53.436 --> 03:10:57.396
removing it from sight. We believe New Zealand can do better than that.

2322
03:10:58.216 --> 03:11:01.856
We can choose responses that are practical, evidence-based, and humane.

2323
03:11:02.436 --> 03:11:05.976
We can choose responses that promote the flourishing and well-being of

2324
03:11:06.036 --> 03:11:09.476
individuals and whanau while strengthening our communities.

2325
03:11:10.956 --> 03:11:14.916
Whether we approach this from a faith perspective or simply ordinary

2326
03:11:14.976 --> 03:11:17.596
common sense, the conclusion is the same.

2327
03:11:17.846 --> 03:11:21.836
This bill risks criminalizing vulnerability rather than responding to

2328
03:11:21.876 --> 03:11:22.016
it.

2329
03:11:23.016 --> 03:11:26.736
As we were preparing for today, I sat with this issue and I was

2330
